# The exact tool versions this course is verified against.
#
# This file is the single place the required versions are written down. Both
# environment check scripts read it, so a version can not be raised in one
# place and left stale in the other.
#
# KEY=VALUE with no quoting or expansion, because it has to be read by POSIX
# sh and by PowerShell without either needing a parser.
#
# RENODE_VERSION is pinned rather than floating because
# boards/nucleo_f401re.repl inherits platforms/cpus/stm32f4.repl from the
# Renode installation. That file is maintained upstream and can change without
# this repository changing, so the simulator version is part of the board's
# definition and not merely part of the toolchain.
#
# 1.16.1 rather than the current 1.17.0, for now, on two grounds: it is the
# version the feasibility spike verified, and 1.17.0 renamed its release assets
# in a way that has already broken Antmicro's own Dockerfile. Moving to 1.17.0
# is a deliberate change with its own verification, not a routine bump.
#
# A third ground used to be listed and was wrong: that 1.17.0 removed the Intel
# macOS packages. It did not remove them, because 1.16.1 does not have them
# either -- checked against both release pages on 2026-10-09. The last release
# with an Intel macOS package was 1.16.0. Staying on 1.16.1 buys nothing for
# Intel Macs, which is why NATIVE-SETUP.md sends them to the container.

RENODE_VERSION=1.16.1
RENODE_DOWNLOAD=https://github.com/renode/renode/releases/tag/v1.16.1

ARM_GCC_VERSION=14.2.Rel1
ARM_GCC_COMMAND=arm-none-eabi-gcc
ARM_GCC_DOWNLOAD=https://developer.arm.com/downloads/-/arm-gnu-toolchain-downloads
